<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron plans convenience stores.</title>
<headline>Petron plans convenience stores.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine oil refiner Petron Corp said on Wednesday it planned to put up convenience stores in its gasoline outlets as part of the company's strategy to beef-up market share.</p>
<p>&quot;We are doing it on our own, there are no tie-ups,&quot; Petron chairman Monico Jacob told reporters.</p>
<p>Petron has about 1,000 gasoline stations nationwide.</p>
<p>Earlier, Uniwide Holdings Inc had expressed interest in setting up convenience stores in Petron's service stations, Petron officials said.</p>
<p>Fastfood chain Jollibee Foods Corp was also reported to be interested in setting up hamburger chains in its stations.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
